<section class="section limits-section" id="limitations" aria-labelledby="limits-title">
  <div class="limits-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="kicker">04 · Scope boundary</p>
      <h2 id="limits-title">What StereoPatch does—and <em>does not</em> establish.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="limits-copy">
      <p>
        StereoPatch forms an RGB-indexed policy condition by retrieving registered DeFM
        evidence before action decoding. Across the matched fixed-base protocols, the full
        interface records higher observed success than the tested modality, fusion, and
        relative-position controls.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Distinctions absent from the frozen RGB or depth fields cannot be recovered by fusion alone.</li>
        <li>The resolution sweep identifies a tested operating point, not a monotonic law.</li>
        <li>Action-response maps measure sensitivity, not directional correctness.</li>
        <li>Mobile manipulation, navigation, coupled viewpoint change, and broader workspace variation remain untested.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

